{
  "dom_id": "step-30876",
  "name": "Using Eigenvalues to Classify Quadratic Forms",
  "problem": "Given a quadratic form $Q(\\mathbf x) = \\mathbf{x}^T A \\mathbf{x}$ with a symmetric matrix $A$,  we have the following theorem:\n\n- $Q$ is positive-definite if and only if all the eigenvalues of $A$ are positive,\n\n- $Q$ is positive semi-definite if and only if all the eigenvalues of $A$ are non-negative,\n\n- $Q$ is negative-definite if and only if all the eigenvalues of $A$ are negative,\n\n- $Q$ is negative semi-definite if and only if all the eigenvalues of $A$ are non-positive,\n\n- $Q$ is indefinite if and only if $A$ has both positive and negative eigenvalues.\n\nUsing the same criteria, we can also classify the symmetric matrix $A$ as positive-definite, positive semi-definite, etc.\n\nFor example, consider the matrix $A,$ given by\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14169381/assets/8582c8b840b1e4696b9f83cb2c117d67e3b832e40b1ded716e0dcd23752c6f9c.svg)\n\nComputing the characteristic equation of $A,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|A-\\lambda I| & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}-5-\\lambda  & -1 \\\\ -1 & -5-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-5-\\lambda )(-5-\\lambda )-1 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}+10\\lambda +24 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +4)(\\lambda +6) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda  & =-4,\\,-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince all the eigenvalues of $A$ are negative, the quadratic form $Q(\\mathbf x) =  \\mathbf{x}^T A \\, \\mathbf{x}$ (as well as the matrix $A$) is negative-definite.",
  "worked_solution": "",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
  "html": "<div id=\"step-30876\" class=\"step\" style=\"display: block\" stepid=\"30876\" steptype=\"tutorial\" contentid=\"4952\">\n            <div class=\"stepHeader\">\n                <div class=\"stepName\">\n                    <a id=\"stepAnchor-30876\" class=\"stepAnchor\" name=\"step-6\">Using Eigenvalues to Classify Quadratic Forms</a>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"helpButton\" stepid=\"30876\">?</div>\n            </div> \n\n            <style type=\"text/css\">\n                            .mjpage .MJX-monospace {\n                            font-family: monospace\n                            }\n\n                            .mjpage .MJX-sans-serif {\n                            font-family: sans-serif\n                            }\n\n                            .mjpage {\n                            display: inline;\n                            font-style: normal;\n                            font-weight: normal;\n                            line-height: normal;\n                            font-size: 100%;\n                            font-size-adjust: none;\n                            text-indent: 0;\n                            text-align: left;\n                            text-transform: none;\n                            letter-spacing: normal;\n                            word-spacing: normal;\n                            word-wrap: normal;\n                            white-space: nowrap;\n                            float: none;\n                            direction: ltr;\n                            max-width: none;\n                            max-height: none;\n                            min-width: 0;\n                            min-height: 0;\n                            border: 0;\n                            padding: 0;\n                            margin: 0\n                            }\n\n                            .mjpage * {\n                            transition: none;\n                            -webkit-transition: none;\n                            -moz-transition: none;\n                            -ms-transition: none;\n                            -o-transition: none\n                            }\n\n                            .mjx-svg-href {\n                            fill: blue;\n                            stroke: blue\n                            }\n\n                            .MathJax_SVG_LineBox {\n                            display: table!important\n                            }\n\n                            .MathJax_SVG_LineBox span {\n                            display: table-cell!important;\n                            width: 10000em!important;\n                            min-width: 0;\n                            max-width: none;\n                            padding: 0;\n                            border: 0;\n                            margin: 0\n                            }\n\n                            .mjpage__block {\n                            text-align: center;\n                            margin: 1em 0em;\n                            position: relative;\n                            display: block!important;\n                            text-indent: 0;\n                            max-width: none;\n                            max-height: none;\n                            min-width: 0;\n                            min-height: 0;\n                            width: 100%\n                            }</style><p>Given a quadratic form <span class=\"mjpage\"><svg xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" width=\"14.111ex\" height=\"3.009ex\" style=\"vertical-align: -0.838ex;\" viewBox=\"0 -934.9 6075.7 1295.7\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" aria-labelledby=\"MathJax-SVG-1-Title\">\n<title id=\"MathJax-SVG-1-Title\">Q(\\mathbf x) = \\mathbf{x}^T A \\mathbf{x}</title>\n<defs aria-hidden=\"true\">\n<path stroke-width=\"1\" id=\"E1-MJMATHI-51\" d=\"M399 -80Q399 -47 400 -30T402 -11V-7L387 -